From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lef <me@lefteros.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:00:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: samsung,s2mpg15-pmic: the sub-PMIC is on
 Tensor G3 and G4

The Pixel 8 Pro (Tensor G3) has an S2MPG15 sub-PMIC too, with the same
three GNSS LDOs, as its zuma-husky node shows. Say G3 and G4 in the
descriptions of the PMIC and of its regulators. No property changes.

Signed-off-by: Lef <me@lefteros.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg15-pmic.yaml | 2 +-
 .../bindings/regulator/samsung,s2mpg15-regulator.yaml           | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg15-pmic.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg15-pmic.yaml
index 90d7e8442..0d6ba7675 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg15-pmic.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/samsung,s2mpg15-pmic.yaml
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ maintainers:
   - W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
 
 description: |
-  S2MPG15 is the sub PMIC paired with Google's Tensor G4 and is reached
+  S2MPG15 is the sub PMIC paired with Google's Tensor G3 and G4 and is reached
   through ACPM. Its LDOs supply the AoC sensors, the GNSS receiver, the
   camera sensors and the fingerprint sensor.
   Interrupt, meter, GPIO and RTC functions are not described here.
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/samsung,s2mpg15-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/samsung,s2mpg15-regulator.yaml
index 413415753..b2afeff2d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/samsung,s2mpg15-regulator.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/samsung,s2mpg15-regulator.yaml
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ maintainers:
   - W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
 
 description: |
-  The sub-PMIC paired with Google's Tensor G4. LDO5S and LDO7S supply the
+  The sub-PMIC paired with Google's Tensor G3 and G4. LDO5S and LDO7S supply the
   AoC sensors, LDO9S, LDO10S and LDO11S the GNSS receiver's core, RF front
   end and auxiliary supply, LDO12S the camera sensors' 1.8 V and LDO15S the
   fingerprint sensor's 3.3 V. Enable control and voltage readback are
